    {
      "s": 4.05,
      "e": 8.77,
      "text": "A lot of times you'll adjust the stitches per inch depending on the project and the strength"
    },
    {
      "s": 8.77,
      "e": 12.57,
      "text": "that the material needs to have."
    },
    {
      "s": 12.57,
      "e": 16.53,
      "text": "So if it's like a load bearing stitch you really want to have a lot of stitches per inch"
    },
    {
      "s": 16.53,
      "e": 18.85,
      "text": "more strength."
    },
    {
      "s": 18.85,
      "e": 22.85,
      "text": "Less stitches per inch just means you want to get those two pieces together."
    },
    {
      "s": 22.85,
      "e": 26.85,
      "text": "It doesn't really have to take any kind of load or have a whole ton of strength but it"
    },
    {
      "s": 26.85,
      "e": 33.89,
      "text": "just binds two pieces together."
    }
  ],
